caption:
Extremely proud of what my team was able to accomplish this weekend. So many people have seen what I’ve been working towards these last few months. Here are some things you should know about my team who joined me this weekend:

@francois_duke sacrificed well over 250 hours over the past year helping me get back into top shape. I could go on about this guy forever, but he’s the best friend any person could ask for.

@jameslifee and I grabbed coffee last September and talked about what I wanted to do with @htgrcanada . I could still barely walk, but instead of looking at me like I was crazy he jumped on board no hesitation. He finished his first marathon this weekend after legitimately collapsing at about the 30km point. His resilience is unmatched.

@woodside84 completed his first ever marathon in a staggering 3hr15mins. This guy is an absolute athletic beast and constantly motivates me to be better with his dedication to hard work and his constant positive attitude.

@nickgiams -The guy with the biggest traps probably to ever run a marathon. G came in at the start of the training process with a chip on his shoulders and absolutely did not disappoint. Seeing his finish Sunday put tears in my eyes for the first time since grade school.

@brendanlacelle –Crazy to see his progress throughout our training. This guy was so incredibly focused on growth it was admirable. An amazing guy who I look forward to pushing the pace with for many runs to come.

@alexpennell -A blessing on race day as we ran the entire 42.2kms together. Without his support the 35km wall would have been so much harder to run through. Excited to coerce him into another long run next year.

@vincentduquette12 showed up with NO training and finished the full marathon with us. Blows my mind every time I think about it. His mental toughness is unmatched.

Shout outs to: @jeffgraham21 and @samgoose9 for pushing through their first half with us on Sunday. @diane.hardman , @paigeemorgann_ @samanthatrickey and @alanaakking for biking/keeping us alive all 42kms! And a big thanks to the volunteers who set up aid stations and cheered us on as well🤗

Can’t wait to see what this atypical group gets up to next.
